{
  "updated_at": "2026-10-30 10:04 JST",
  "total": 50,
  "toyota_summary": "European automakers reported strong electric vehicle sales this quarter, undercutting their own argument that tighter emissions rules threaten their competitiveness. The industry has lobbied hard for weaker EU regulations, claiming they cannot meet current targets without crippling investment. Rising EV demand exposes this claim as overstated and will make it harder to win regulatory relief from Brussels.\n\nThe political problem runs deeper than quarterly numbers. When automakers simultaneously argue that emissions rules are impossible to meet and report surging EV sales, regulators stop listening. This weakens the industry's leverage on every future negotiation over fuel economy, battery standards, and the pace of combustion engine phase-outs. A credibility gap this wide takes years to repair.\n\nWatch whether automakers shift their messaging away from compliance doom and toward supply chain or profitability arguments instead.",
